{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"task-board q --format compact 'get(TASK-260720-1nvomm) { full }'\"","aggregated_output":"id:TASK-260720-1nvomm\ntype:task\nname:protocol-v6-core-security-contract\ntitle:Specify protocol v6 core and security contract\nstatus:analysis\nreview:required\ntask_class:code\nestimate:{\"kind\":\"estimated\",\"scale\":{\"kind\":\"fibonacci\",\"number\":5}}\nobservability:{\"readiness\":{\"advisoryBlockedElementIds\":[],\"blockedElementIds\":[],\"coverage\":{\"complete\":true,\"estimated\":1,\"ratio\":\"1/1\",\"total\":1,\"unestimated\":0},\"estimateKind\":\"estimated\",\"isAdvisoryBlocked\":false,\"isBlocked\":false,\"rolledEstimate\":{\"kind\":\"estimated\",\"scale\":{\"kind\":\"fibonacci\",\"number\":5}}},\"scope\":{\"id\":\"TASK-260720-1nvomm\",\"name\":\"protocol-v6-core-security-contract\",\"type\":\"task\"},\"summary\":{\"active\":[{\"id\":\"TASK-260720-1nvomm\",\"name\":\"protocol-v6-core-security-contract\",\"status\":\"analysis\"}],\"blocked\":[],\"byType\":{\"bug\":{\"total\":0,\"todo\":0,\"active\":0,\"done\":0,\"closed\":0,\"blocked\":0},\"epic\":{\"total\":0,\"todo\":0,\"active\":0,\"done\":0,\"closed\":0,\"blocked\":0},\"story\":{\"total\":0,\"todo\":0,\"active\":0,\"done\":0,\"closed\":0,\"blocked\":0},\"task\":{\"total\":1,\"todo\":0,\"active\":1,\"done\":0,\"closed\":0,\"blocked\":0}}}}\nparent:STORY-260720-35dck7\nassignee:[analyst] solution-architect (codex)\ndescription:Update the normative protocol model from the accepted TASK-260720-poa3ze contract. Define manifest schema 6 as a declarative compiled-artifact extension with build_roots and a closed go-v1 command. Build sources must be statically excluded from agent context and runtime copying on real installs, cache hits, and dry-runs. Record the no-hooks threat boundary, build-source identity, logical cache and receipt semantics, marker v2 compatibility, and the Go-only v1 decision. Preserve every schema 1 through 5 behavior.\nscope:Work only in /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator-spec from origin/main commit 57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730. Own protocol/core.md, SECURITY.md, and new decisions/0004-compile-only-build-drivers.md. Use TASK-260720-poa3ze_compile-only-build-drivers.md at accepted SHA-256 6308d99d8bdad4445841bc1cbd230cadbed0020012d0e9d38d877b413348f681 as the contract. Do not edit schemas, vectors, generator, manager profile, CLI guide, or release metadata in this task.\nac:protocol/core.md normatively defines schema 6, build_roots, the strict build command, build-source exclusion, manager-derived artifact paths, curator-build-source-v1, logical cache and receipt identity, marker v2 implications, and schema 1 through 5 compatibility; SECURITY.md explicitly forbids package shell, argv, environment, output selection, hooks, plugins, generators, unsafe build systems, external-link fallback, and executing built output while documenting compiler-input and protected-cache trust boundaries; decision 0004 records the closed Go-only v1 choice, rejected alternatives, non-normative physical cache layout, and future-driver review rule; terminology matches the accepted contract without weakening any MUST or MUST NOT; python3 tools/validate.py passes.\nblockedBy:[]\nblocks:[\"TASK-260720-17llva\",\"TASK-260720-wajgn8\"]\nderivedBlockedBy:[]\nderivedBlocks:[]\nchecklist:[{\"text\":\"Map every accepted protocol decision and security boundary to normative prose or decision 0004\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Prove build roots are excluded from agent context and runtime copying on real, cache-hit, and dry-run paths\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Run the scoped protocol validation command and record the result\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Code written per task description and AC\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Lint clean\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Implementation matches AC\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Solution fits project architecture\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Tests green\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Board size is proportional to the spec and is the smallest decomposition that maps every requirement\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"Every story and task traces to a concrete spec requirement; justified-gap elements also carry a self-verified gap record\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"Beyond-literal-spec elements include a written justification naming the gap and the spec and out-of-scope checks performed before creation\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"Research tasks cite an exact question the spec genuinely leaves open\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"Dependencies linked\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"Tasks are atomic — one clear deliverable each\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"Completeness verified — nothing forgotten\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"Any planning artifacts actually produced are linked as new task-scoped outcome resources; diagrams are strictly optional, never a standing deliverable\",\"done\":false}]\nnotes:spawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-bc3052, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-bc3052)\\nImplemented the accepted schema-6 core/security contract from the verified 6308d99d... input on a clean branch rooted at required origin/main 57c1f568.... Decision and threat-boundary findings are recorded in decisions/0004 and TASK-260720-1nvomm_results.md. This is a documentation-only owned scope: schemas/vectors/tests are downstream-owned and were not edited; existing validation passed. The host Python initially lacked jsonschema, so validation used a task-local venv populated from pinned requirements-dev.txt.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-bc3052, pid=1744, exit=0)\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-9fca47, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-9fca47)\\nReview verdict: changes requested. protocol/core.md weakens two accepted MUST-level details: bootstrap probes do not explicitly use a manager-owned empty CWD with GOENV=off and GOTOOLCHAIN=local in the bootstrap environment, and go-list trust does not require the accepted Standard && Goroot conjunction. Full evidence and green validation results are in TASK-260720-1nvomm_review-verdict.md. Route to documentation rework, then a new reviewer cycle.\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-9fca47, pid=16192, exit=0)\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-d7e0fe, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-d7e0fe)\\nReviewer rework applied in protocol/core.md: bootstrap probes now use a manager-owned empty CWD with private roots, GOENV=off, GOTOOLCHAIN=local, normalized locale, and no inherited GOROOT/target; go-list toolchain trust now requires Standard == true and Goroot == true. Scoped validator and full make validate pass in the pinned task-local venv; git diff --check passes. Updated TASK-260720-1nvomm_results.md and TASK-260720-1nvomm_validation.log with exact evidence.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn completion blocked: no new task-scoped outcome artifact was attached. Add an outcome resource named like TASK-260720-1nvomm_results.md and then set status back to to-review.\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-d7e0fe, pid=24410, exit=0)\\nOrchestrator recovery: content rework is complete and validated, but RUN-260720-d7e0fe could not hand off because it updated existing outcome resources instead of attaching a distinct new task-scoped rework outcome. Add a new TASK-260720-1nvomm_rework-1.md outcome resource containing the two corrections and exact validation evidence; do not change project files unless evidence is inaccurate; then route to to-review.\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-b95c7d, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-b95c7d)\\nRecovery audit confirmed both reviewer-requested MUST-level corrections and found one additional accepted-contract gap: dependency command narrowing still said script-only. protocol/core.md now permits schema-6 build commands while explicitly retaining script-only behavior for schemas 1 through 5. Evidence is attached as TASK-260720-1nvomm_rework-1.md; scoped and combined validation gates pass.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-b95c7d, pid=37242, exit=0)\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-e7562d, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-e7562d)\\nFinal review verdict: accepted. All acceptance criteria and accepted-contract decisions are covered in the three owned documents; prior MUST-level gaps and legacy dependency narrowing are corrected. Independent scoped and full validation gates pass. Evidence attached as TASK-260720-1nvomm_review-2.md.\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-e7562d, pid=43454, exit=0)\\nScope delta requested 2026-07-27: add first-class external build-repository dependencies for Go CLI commands, with later closed drivers for other languages. This is a genuine architecture deci